{
  "notes": "Tiling deployment contract conformance cases (usermanual metadata.md#tiling, conversion/calibration.md#geometry-check). metadata_invalid entries are documents a producer (trainer or converter) must never emit; each applies an RFC 7386 JSON merge patch to the named metadata_valid entry and 'error' is a regular expression searched in the expected error message. Snapshot resize values are letterbox | stretch | tiled. A model without a version-1 tiling section accepts letterbox or stretch snapshots, and tiled snapshots whose params carry a legacy 'tiling' mapping (ModelPack tiled snapshots). Consumers (runtimes) are lenient instead: they ignore unknown keys and, for an unsupported tiling.version, warn and treat the block as absent. converter_tiling entries place 'tiling' at edgefirst['tiling'] (the key is present) and a converter must reject every one with a non-null 'error' (regular expression searched in the message) and accept the null ones; an absent 'tiling' key is always accepted. snapshot_geometry 'error': null means the check must pass, and 'full_frame' is the model's tiling.full_frame.enabled (false when absent).",
